    "claim": "Nebula key doctrine: every private key lives under runtime/nebula/networks/<name>/ (gitignored by the repo), the CA key never leaves the owning instance, and member cert+key travel only as join_network parameters over the already-encrypted peer channel. The 2023 code has one wart to fix: create_network and add_member stage ca.key/certs through the process working directory (rename/copy dance) instead of using nebula-cert's -ca-key/-ca-crt/-out-crt/-out-key flags — a crash mid-command leaves a CA key in the checkout root.",
